Feature: Losing the TX15
  If the serial line goes quiet, the flight computer does the same as a receiver that lost
  its link. It sets the throttle channel below the failsafe level of ArduPilot. ArduPilot then
  starts its [[failsafe]].

  Expectation: A quiet line is a failsafe
    Given the TX15 throttle stick is 50 %
    When the TX15 is not connected
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the throttle channel is at most 900 us
    And the TX15 uplink quality is 0 %

  Expectation: The plane flies again when the TX15 comes back
    Given the TX15 is not connected
    And the TX15 throttle stick is 50 %
    When the TX15 is connected
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the throttle channel is at least 1490 us
    And the TX15 uplink quality is 100 %
